      "message": "\u003e This is because we added some other files in some directories and we have to pack them when generating bugreport.\n\nwhy do you \"have to\"? i mean, if they\u0027re in different directories to start with (good!), why do you have to put them in the same directory in the zip file (bad!)? that seems confusing and/or like you\u0027re throwing away information (since i\u0027m assuming these two files in different directories on the device\u0027s filesystem aren\u0027t actually _identical_, otherwise there would be no point).\n\nif you were saying you wanted to make the device\u0027s command-line zip/unzip tools behave more like the traditional desktop ones, with all the UI that lets you choose what to do with duplicates, on a case-by-case basis, that would be more convincingly a good idea. but no-one\u0027s asked for _that_ yet :-)\n\nthis just seems like we\u0027re adding a way to make it easier for people to mistakenly lose data/confuse themselves about _which_ data they actually have in the file. (especially if you imagine multiple teams being responsible for the different copies!)",
